\begin{abstract}
The Autonomous Dark Domain Engine (ADDE-v4) is a sovereign, distributed
computational framework integrating encrypted astrophysical data ingestion,
large-scale cosmological simulation, and dark-sector anomaly detection within a
single unified architecture. The system combines AMR+PM+Octree N-body
gravitational solvers with CKKS fully homomorphic encryption, enabling
privacy-preserving evaluation of weak-lensing shear fields, BAO correlation
functions, and generative anomaly metrics across 16{,}384 encrypted SIMD slots.
Empirical validation demonstrates numerical stability at $16{,}384^3$ particle
resolution, InfiniBand saturation at $97.8\%$, and automated cryptographic
bootstrapping recovery at multiplicative depth~12. Under extreme observational
conditions---including $30\%$ intrinsic shape noise and $25\%$ masking---ADDE-v4
reconstructs convergence maps with $\mathrm{SNR}=8.42$ and detects injected
dark-sector perturbations at $5.12\sigma$ significance. These results establish
ADDE-v4 as a fully validated, real-time, privacy-preserving cosmological engine
capable of supporting next-generation dark matter and dark energy discovery
across live survey pipelines.
\end{abstract}